body: "## Why\n\nOn npm, `pm-gantt-chart` links **Homepage** to `https://github.com/unbraind/pm-gantt-chart#readme`, the same place as the Repository link beside it. The package has its page in the pm cli package catalog: https://pm-cli.unbrained.dev/packages/pm-gantt-chart. Pointing npm there gives people a useful place to land and lets search engines tie the package to its website. The author field (`\"@unbraind\"`) has no link to the person behind the work.\n\n## What to change\n\nIn `package.json`:\n\n```json\n\"homepage\": \"https://pm-cli.unbrained.dev/packages/pm-gantt-chart\",\n\"author\": { \"name\": \"unbrained\", \"url\": \"https://unbrained.dev/about\" },\n```\n\n- Currently: `\"homepage\": \"https://github.com/unbraind/pm-gantt-chart#readme\"`, `\"author\": \"@unbraind\"`.\n- Keep `repository` and `bugs` as they are.\n- Set the repository's GitHub website (About → Website) to the same address (currently empty): `gh repo edit unbraind/pm-gantt-chart --homepage https://pm-cli.unbrained.dev/packages/pm-gantt-chart`.\n- npm takes the new fields with the next published version.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- [ ] `npm view pm-gantt-chart homepage` prints `https://pm-cli.unbrained.dev/packages/pm-gantt-chart` after the next release.\n- [ ] `npm view pm-gantt-chart author` includes the url `https://unbrained.dev/about`.\n- [ ] The GitHub repository's website is `https://pm-cli.unbrained.dev/packages/pm-gantt-chart`.\n\n## Context\n\nChecked 2026-10-25 with `npm view` and the GitHub API. The same change has been filed in every published unbrained package's repository (pm-cli as unbraind/pm-cli#1594, its extensions, pm-web and the agent-ready clis), so they all link the same way: the product page as homepage, https://unbrained.dev/about as the author."
